-- title:
--   Relative degree at most ℓ+1 for Γ_H(N)∩Γ₀(Nℓ)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, $N$ a nonzero natural number, $\ell$ a prime, and suppose that the image of $N\ell$ in $K$ is nonzero and that $\ell \nmid N$; let $H$ be a subgroup of $(\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$. Write $\Gamma_H(N) \le \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ for [`CohCarrier.GammaH N H`](def/CohCarrier_Level.html#L133), the image in $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb{Z})$ of the preimage of $H$ under the homomorphism $\Gamma_0(N) \to (\mathbb{Z}/N)^\times$ attached to the reduction of the lower-right entry (with inverse the reduction of the upper-left entry). For a subgroup $\Gamma$, [`ModularCurve.qExpFunctionFieldC K Γ`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L101) is the intermediate field of $K((q))/K$ generated by the set of quotients $\mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_f / \mathrm{intSeriesC}\,K\,p_g$, where $f,g$ are modular forms of some weight $k$ for the image of $\Gamma$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(\mathbb{R})$ admitting integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g \in \mathbb{Z}[[q]]$ and the denominator series is nonzero in $K((q))$. The assertion is that the relative degree of `qExpFunctionFieldC K (GammaH N H ⊓ Gamma0 (N*ℓ))` over `qExpFunctionFieldC K (GammaH N H)` is at most $\ell+1$ and is strictly positive; since the relative degree of intermediate fields is $0$ for infinite extensions, the second clause expresses finiteness.
--
--   This is the field-theoretic counterpart of the index computation $[\Gamma_H(N):\Gamma_H(N)\cap\Gamma_0(N\ell)] = \ell+1$ for $\ell \nmid N$, stated for $q$-expansion function fields over an arbitrary base field in which $N\ell$ is invertible. It is used in the comparison of the function field of $\Gamma_H(N)\cap\Gamma_0(N\ell)$ with the field generated over that of $\Gamma_H(N)$ by the $q$-expansion of $j$ at the $\ell$-isogeny level.
-- source:
